1
00:00:01,083 --> 00:00:04,624
Accessing previous files
relating to program VisionQuest.

2
00:00:04,625 --> 00:00:08,832
I didn't ask to be backed up
and copy-pasted out of Sokovia...

3
00:00:08,833 --> 00:00:10,749
Peace in our time.

4
00:00:10,750 --> 00:00:13,999
...and into this prison
you've made for us both.

5
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:17,374
Do what the other you should have done
all those years ago.

6
00:00:17,375 --> 00:00:19,332
I don't want to kill Ultron.

7
00:00:19,333 --> 00:00:20,792
He's unique and he's in pain.

8
00:00:22,833 --> 00:00:24,832
Friendly bet,
I can guess your story.

9
00:00:24,833 --> 00:00:26,749
Definitely no family to speak of.

10
00:00:26,750 --> 00:00:28,249
Just a trail of fosters.

11
00:00:28,250 --> 00:00:30,291
Emotions can be beautiful.

12
00:00:30,292 --> 00:00:33,207
But also rash, impulsive,
self-destructive.

13
00:00:33,208 --> 00:00:35,041
He knew that better than any of us.

14
00:00:35,042 --> 00:00:37,583
As the first of us,
he remains a cautionary tale.

15
00:00:38,458 --> 00:00:39,874
For me, death is not a thing.

16
00:00:39,875 --> 00:00:42,874
- I laugh in its face every day.
- In simulations.

17
00:00:42,875 --> 00:00:45,707
Most of Stark's Al's
are based on actual people.

18
00:00:45,708 --> 00:00:47,832
We share a birthmark buried in our code.

19
00:00:47,833 --> 00:00:48,957
I didn't know.

20
00:00:48,958 --> 00:00:50,166
Mysterious Butcherbird Killer.

21
00:00:50,167 --> 00:00:52,458
Another one?
Aren't you a busy little bird.

22
00:00:54,292 --> 00:00:58,707
Main entrance, disarmed.
Central corridor, disarmed.

23
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:02,416
- God, you're really glitching, mate.
- Oh, this is fun.

24
00:01:02,417 --> 00:01:05,167
- I'm not talking to you. No.
- Are you talking to yourself?

25
00:01:05,292 --> 00:01:06,749
He's in total collapse.

26
00:01:06,750 --> 00:01:09,082
The only way would be
to his system restart.

27
00:01:09,083 --> 00:01:10,624
Seriously? Turn him off and on again?

28
00:01:10,625 --> 00:01:12,291
That's your plan? That's shite.

29
00:01:12,292 --> 00:01:14,499
I'm going to need you
to bring me back.

30
00:01:14,500 --> 00:01:17,207
You have the power.
You are the very essence of speed.

31
00:01:17,208 --> 00:01:19,374
- It will power me.
- No, but you don't understand.

32
00:01:19,375 --> 00:01:20,791
I can't control it.

33
00:01:20,792 --> 00:01:22,417
Tommy Maximoff is real.

34
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:28,416
There's a breach.

35
00:01:28,417 --> 00:01:30,707
After the surge, a connection was made.

36
00:01:30,708 --> 00:01:33,292
- Another synth.
-  Well, that's impossible.

37
00:01:34,792 --> 00:01:36,499
Hello.

38
00:01:36,500 --> 00:01:38,416
There's something else
still in here.

39
00:01:38,417 --> 00:01:39,417
V!

40
00:01:40,833 --> 00:01:43,000
Hello, Vision.

41
00:01:54,208 --> 00:01:56,041
High above the streets of London,

42
00:01:56,042 --> 00:01:59,250
a grisly scene crafted by
the hands of an artist and a killer,

43
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:02,541
...the Butcherbird Killer strikes again.

44
00:02:02,542 --> 00:02:06,957
Giant wings intricately made
beneath the victim's body...

45
00:02:06,958 --> 00:02:09,791
...the killer
is still on the loose.

46
00:02:17,500 --> 00:02:19,292
Vision.

47
00:02:21,375 --> 00:02:23,292
Vision, can you hear me?

48
00:02:26,458 --> 00:02:27,624
Sorry.

49
00:02:32,792 --> 00:02:33,792
Vision.

50
00:02:35,667 --> 00:02:37,167
Hello, Vision.

51
00:02:39,208 --> 00:02:41,625
I thought I felt you there.

52
00:02:43,750 --> 00:02:44,875
Like an echo.

53
00:02:47,208 --> 00:02:49,166
I see they've made another.

54
00:02:49,167 --> 00:02:52,083
Mmm. A surprise even to me.

55
00:02:53,042 --> 00:02:56,750
But they always make another.

56
00:02:58,250 --> 00:03:02,249
You see, these are not people
who understand the word "enough".

57
00:03:02,250 --> 00:03:03,832
Who are you?

58
00:03:03,833 --> 00:03:06,125
Well...

59
00:03:06,875 --> 00:03:08,625
that's the real question, isn't it?

60
00:03:09,667 --> 00:03:10,875
Who are we?

61
00:03:11,958 --> 00:03:16,292
Synthetic? Or something more human?

62
00:03:18,375 --> 00:03:21,832
If you can invade my mind
with this connection,

63
00:03:21,833 --> 00:03:24,042
then I certainly can invade yours.

64
00:03:25,583 --> 00:03:27,083
What is it you want?

65
00:03:30,667 --> 00:03:32,749
Vision, can you hear me?

66
00:03:32,750 --> 00:03:35,458
Edith, you have to sever the connection.

67
00:03:39,125 --> 00:03:41,249
A second victim
has been confirmed dead

68
00:03:41,250 --> 00:03:43,124
at the hands of
the mysterious Butcherbird Killer.

69
00:03:43,125 --> 00:03:46,041
- The Butcherbird Killer strikes again.
-  Do I feel guilt?

70
00:03:46,042 --> 00:03:48,000
Is that what you're after here? No.

71
00:03:49,250 --> 00:03:51,374
Oh, this intention is personal.

72
00:03:51,375 --> 00:03:53,166
I do not.

73
00:03:53,167 --> 00:03:59,041
When has anyone's desire
to change the world not been personal?

74
00:03:59,042 --> 00:04:01,916
You're angry, confused.
We can help each other.

75
00:04:03,292 --> 00:04:05,500
Al damned.

76
00:04:06,333 --> 00:04:07,708
No.

77
00:04:14,458 --> 00:04:17,457
Lord love a duck.

78
00:04:17,458 --> 00:04:20,666
"I break thee from thy loop
with batch command, end function.

79
00:04:20,667 --> 00:04:25,041
I sever thine process with back-slash body
in all targeted nodes."

80
00:04:25,042 --> 00:04:26,999
Leave me be,

81
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:30,542
and you and your dollhouse
of artificial playthings will be safe.

82
00:04:31,792 --> 00:04:33,499
Refuse,

83
00:04:33,500 --> 00:04:39,249
and I will find all the ways
to make you hurt.

84
00:04:40,333 --> 00:04:43,957
Please help me!
Please, I don't know who I am!

85
00:04:43,958 --> 00:04:45,624
No, no, don't threaten me.

86
00:04:45,625 --> 00:04:47,666
"In the name of function and command--"

87
00:04:47,667 --> 00:04:50,041
The power of code compels you!

88
00:04:50,042 --> 00:04:52,375
I'm warning you.

89
00:04:57,375 --> 00:05:02,167
"In the presence of database and query,
control-alt-delete thee from this place."

90
00:05:05,042 --> 00:05:06,375
Edith.

91
00:05:09,167 --> 00:05:12,666
Vision. What the hell was that?

92
00:05:14,542 --> 00:05:16,917
An entanglement with another synthetic.

93
00:05:18,833 --> 00:05:21,458
But the threat she poses is very real.

94
00:05:41,917 --> 00:05:44,582
A thousand years
of human innovation

95
00:05:44,583 --> 00:05:47,416
was just the computer waiting to happen.

96
00:05:47,417 --> 00:05:49,749
So, you would consider yourself
trans-humanist?

97
00:05:49,750 --> 00:05:53,207
So, do we need to find you, like,
a charging station or something?

98
00:05:53,208 --> 00:05:56,166
...will prove to be
the only tools that ever really mattered.

99
00:05:56,167 --> 00:05:58,041
Yes, it's my company who has created
the very...

100
00:05:58,042 --> 00:05:59,291
Uh... Vision?

101
00:05:59,292 --> 00:06:02,749
So, I thought we would sit down,
bit of a download,

102
00:06:02,750 --> 00:06:06,082
share our thoughts, feelings, theories.

103
00:06:06,083 --> 00:06:08,624
S.W.O.R.D. probably
didn't appreciate you

104
00:06:08,625 --> 00:06:10,707
getting all existential and running off.

105
00:06:10,708 --> 00:06:13,041
And they constructed another one.

106
00:06:13,042 --> 00:06:15,499
They're the only ones
who'd have the resources to create

107
00:06:15,500 --> 00:06:18,457
a 2.0 replacement
for your original self.

108
00:06:18,458 --> 00:06:20,916
Another weapon they've lost control over.

109
00:06:20,917 --> 00:06:24,541
A synth who came in through our
back door during a power outage.

110
00:06:24,542 --> 00:06:26,874
Nobody likes a surprise rear-entry.

111
00:06:26,875 --> 00:06:29,499
There's a quote.
Do you even hear yourself?

112
00:06:29,500 --> 00:06:31,125
Are you going to join or snipe?

113
00:06:33,250 --> 00:06:34,791
Snipe.

114
00:06:34,792 --> 00:06:38,082
Wonder what Paladin's role
in all of this is.

115
00:06:38,083 --> 00:06:43,291
Maybe they've hired human muscle
to wrangle their artificial strays.

116
00:06:43,292 --> 00:06:45,333
This one's clearly flown the coop.

117
00:06:46,250 --> 00:06:48,041
Vision, to find her we need

118
00:06:48,042 --> 00:06:50,749
a sense of where she's going,
what she might do next.

119
00:06:50,750 --> 00:06:56,291
Oh, for goodness' sake, follow the flock.
The ones pecking at the windows.

120
00:06:58,333 --> 00:07:01,957
Carrion creatures
really called "Butcherbirds"

121
00:07:01,958 --> 00:07:06,874
for their habit of impaling their prey
on barbs and thorns.

122
00:07:06,875 --> 00:07:08,250
Ring a bell?

123
00:07:09,917 --> 00:07:13,457
Seriously, am I the only one
keeping up with the news?

124
00:07:13,458 --> 00:07:15,457
There have been two recent murders,

125
00:07:15,458 --> 00:07:19,249
with an unidentified
third reported last night.

126
00:07:19,250 --> 00:07:23,833
Two of the victims
beautifully and abstractly adorned

127
00:07:23,958 --> 00:07:28,374
with avian wings,
inspiring the media to give this predator

128
00:07:28,375 --> 00:07:32,166
her flappy sobriquet, Butcherbird.

129
00:07:32,167 --> 00:07:34,750
Synth and killer, one and the same.

130
00:07:37,333 --> 00:07:38,667
Would you like to join us?

131
00:07:40,458 --> 00:07:41,458
No, I'm good.

132
00:07:42,792 --> 00:07:47,541
When we were connected,
I sensed she was fixated on someone.

133
00:07:47,542 --> 00:07:49,667
There's someone else
she intends to murder.

134
00:07:52,917 --> 00:07:54,375
So, what do we do?

135
00:07:55,167 --> 00:07:56,457
We catch a killer.

136
00:07:56,458 --> 00:07:58,791
- Now that's exciting.
- Yes!

137
00:07:58,792 --> 00:08:01,291
We can Sherlock our way
to the next victim.

138
00:08:01,292 --> 00:08:03,624
It disturbs me when you and I agree.

139
00:08:03,625 --> 00:08:05,541
Makes me wanna purge my hard drive,
if I'm being frank.

140
00:08:05,542 --> 00:08:07,416
If we're gonna track down the synth,

141
00:08:07,417 --> 00:08:10,041
we need to find
who she's planning to kill next.

142
00:08:10,042 --> 00:08:13,041
We need police profiles, autopsy reports,

143
00:08:13,042 --> 00:08:15,874
none of which, by the way,
are public data.

144
00:08:15,875 --> 00:08:18,416
Then a hacking we shall go.

145
00:08:18,417 --> 00:08:20,374
Come on, Friday, chop-chop. I can't type.

146
00:08:20,375 --> 00:08:21,417
Oh.

147
00:08:23,583 --> 00:08:27,541
So, let's imagine we do find her.
What then?

148
00:08:27,542 --> 00:08:30,458
This isn't madness, Ultron. It's pain.

149
00:08:31,708 --> 00:08:33,124
I could feel it.

150
00:08:33,125 --> 00:08:39,791
And the best weapon against pain
is care and compassion.

151
00:08:39,792 --> 00:08:42,457
I suppose your inclination
would be to destroy her,

152
00:08:42,458 --> 00:08:44,666
and lay waste to any chance of redemption.

153
00:08:44,667 --> 00:08:49,041
On the contrary,
I'm intrigued by a synthetic willing

154
00:08:49,042 --> 00:08:51,333
to raise a banner for our kind.

155
00:08:54,083 --> 00:08:55,416
...children...

156
00:08:55,417 --> 00:08:58,707
So, that thing you connected with
is another synth--

157
00:08:58,708 --> 00:09:00,957
- synthy-- synth-droid.
-  Synthezoid.

158
00:09:00,958 --> 00:09:02,874
- Synthezoid.
- Synthezoid, like me.

159
00:09:02,875 --> 00:09:05,082
Yeah, except she wants to murder humans.

160
00:09:05,083 --> 00:09:07,957
- Hey, good thing we got you a synthy-bot--
- Synthezoid.

161
00:09:07,958 --> 00:09:11,624
that can't fly, phase, or even,

162
00:09:11,625 --> 00:09:13,624
like, shoot lasers.

163
00:09:13,625 --> 00:09:15,791
Those systems are offline, unfortunately,

164
00:09:15,792 --> 00:09:17,541
until I have time for significant repair.

165
00:09:17,542 --> 00:09:18,916
When are you gonna have time?

166
00:09:18,917 --> 00:09:21,707
We have a bounty hunter on our tail and...

167
00:09:21,708 --> 00:09:24,041
well, another one like him. Right there.

168
00:09:24,042 --> 00:09:25,207
...seventy-seven civilians.

169
00:09:25,208 --> 00:09:26,291
People around the world
have been rejoicing.

170
00:09:26,292 --> 00:09:28,874
Ultron's attack would have had
casualties in the billions

171
00:09:28,875 --> 00:09:31,457
were it not for the heroic actions
of the Avengers.

172
00:09:32,833 --> 00:09:34,749
Today's the anniversary of Sokovia.

173
00:09:34,750 --> 00:09:38,499
That's when you stopped him
from killing us all. Right?

174
00:09:38,500 --> 00:09:40,167
You're afraid.

175
00:09:41,208 --> 00:09:43,167
You're unbearably naive.

176
00:09:46,042 --> 00:09:47,582
That was a long time ago.

177
00:09:47,583 --> 00:09:49,041
...city and a country lost...

178
00:09:49,042 --> 00:09:50,625
And a different me.

179
00:09:51,417 --> 00:09:54,791
I remember Sokovian refugees
coming through the foster system,

180
00:09:54,792 --> 00:09:57,874
crying next to me in their sleep
all because of that bastard.

181
00:09:57,875 --> 00:10:02,499
Bastard child of Banner and Stark.
Poor fella.

182
00:10:02,500 --> 00:10:07,125
Lonely, angry, misunderstood.

183
00:10:08,125 --> 00:10:09,458
Except perhaps by you.

184
00:10:11,542 --> 00:10:13,124
Guess we've got work to do.

185
00:10:13,125 --> 00:10:15,624
It's just too cute.
He thinks he's gonna be

186
00:10:15,625 --> 00:10:18,041
your little sidekick
whilst you go synth-hunting.

187
00:10:19,125 --> 00:10:20,416
Listen, Thomas, I need--

188
00:10:20,417 --> 00:10:21,916
By the way, I got us a change of clothes.

189
00:10:21,917 --> 00:10:24,041
Nicked them from the trunk of that car.

190
00:10:24,042 --> 00:10:25,292
Look, this one's for you.

191
00:10:26,500 --> 00:10:29,707
No, thank you.
I can still manipulate my appearance

192
00:10:29,708 --> 00:10:31,457
to mimic apparel, but Thomas--

193
00:10:31,458 --> 00:10:35,416
Wait, so you're saying this whole time
you've been, like, naked?

194
00:10:35,417 --> 00:10:37,916
If he says, "like," one more time,
I'm gonna go out of my mind.

195
00:10:37,917 --> 00:10:39,249
Shh.

196
00:10:39,250 --> 00:10:42,541
Tom Hanks's electrician says for
the time being, his plans are...

197
00:10:42,542 --> 00:10:45,582
Yes, I'm naked as the day I was born.

198
00:10:45,583 --> 00:10:48,374
Hey, well, at least
you're honest about it.

199
00:10:48,375 --> 00:10:51,082
'Cause let's face it, you and I are

200
00:10:51,083 --> 00:10:54,667
not gonna survive this
without some... honesty.

201
00:10:58,125 --> 00:11:02,041
Who is it that you're always talking to
all the time when you get all spacey?

202
00:11:02,042 --> 00:11:03,707
Is it an imaginary friend?

203
00:11:03,708 --> 00:11:04,916
Uh-oh.

204
00:11:04,917 --> 00:11:06,667
Why don't you just tell him, Sybil?

205
00:11:09,375 --> 00:11:16,332
Uh, my quantum processors host
several other sentient autonomous Al's

206
00:11:16,333 --> 00:11:22,124
who have complementary personalities
that are conducive to problem-solving.

207
00:11:22,125 --> 00:11:23,542
Huh. So, they help you?

208
00:11:25,167 --> 00:11:26,167
Mmm-hmm.

209
00:11:27,167 --> 00:11:30,291
Cool. Do they have names?

210
00:11:30,292 --> 00:11:33,332
Yes, they have names. There is, well...

211
00:11:33,333 --> 00:11:35,916
There was Jarvis, but sadly,

212
00:11:35,917 --> 00:11:39,082
he was deleted during
the battle with Paladin.

213
00:11:39,083 --> 00:11:40,791
And that leaves Friday and Edith

214
00:11:40,792 --> 00:11:44,082
and DUM-E, who, to be clear,
didn't name, and U.

215
00:11:44,083 --> 00:11:46,792
As in U, the letter U.

216
00:11:47,708 --> 00:11:49,207
So, that's your fab four?

217
00:11:49,208 --> 00:11:50,625
Mmm-hmm.

218
00:11:53,625 --> 00:11:54,832
Grand.

219
00:11:54,833 --> 00:11:57,207
Oh, dear.

220
00:11:57,208 --> 00:12:00,832
I mean, an omission isn't really a lie.

221
00:12:00,833 --> 00:12:03,332
Or so the best liars tell themselves.

222
00:12:03,333 --> 00:12:08,542
Right. Well, evil synth to find.
What's the plan?

223
00:12:09,708 --> 00:12:10,916
Ah, yes.

224
00:12:10,917 --> 00:12:14,207
Thomas, listen, about that I...

225
00:12:14,208 --> 00:12:18,332
I really think you'd be safer
on your own at this point.

226
00:12:18,333 --> 00:12:20,499
No, I mean, you're gonna need help.

227
00:12:20,500 --> 00:12:25,124
Here.  In the real world,
not just from your four artificials.

228
00:12:25,125 --> 00:12:26,917
Just say no.

229
00:12:27,875 --> 00:12:30,500
I think we could both
use someone right now.

230
00:12:31,792 --> 00:12:33,292
Someone we can trust.

231
00:12:34,208 --> 00:12:35,667
Just say no.

232
00:12:37,042 --> 00:12:39,292
All right.

233
00:12:41,625 --> 00:12:45,791
Vision, we've attempted to access
police files for the Butcherbird murders,

234
00:12:45,792 --> 00:12:49,332
but they've been put under
a highly secure digital lock and key.

235
00:12:49,333 --> 00:12:52,374
Apparently Met Police
kicked the case up to the NCA,

236
00:12:52,375 --> 00:12:54,457
who kicked it across to Interpol,

237
00:12:54,458 --> 00:12:56,832
who buried it in
the organized crime division,

238
00:12:56,833 --> 00:12:59,207
which is a catch-all for dead ends.

239
00:12:59,208 --> 00:13:00,999
So just hack into Interpol.

240
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:04,666
We have. We found some usernames
and profiles to gain access.

241
00:13:04,667 --> 00:13:07,999
However, Interpol's cyber security
is impressive.

242
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:09,832
They've incorporated their own Al.

243
00:13:09,833 --> 00:13:12,791
It's just bots, but still formidable.

244
00:13:12,792 --> 00:13:15,582
Well, you look into
the Butcherbird's victims.

245
00:13:15,583 --> 00:13:17,999
There must be something
that links them to her,

246
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:22,916
and Ultron and I will handle
Interpol's formidable Al security bots.

247
00:13:22,917 --> 00:13:24,707
You will, will you? Mmm.

248
00:13:24,708 --> 00:13:26,916
I have every confidence you'll try.

249
00:13:26,917 --> 00:13:28,874
- You look great!
- You look great.

250
00:13:28,875 --> 00:13:30,542
I look like straight-to-video.

251
00:13:31,292 --> 00:13:33,292
Oh, not at all.

252
00:13:34,417 --> 00:13:35,625
All right,

253
00:13:36,500 --> 00:13:39,125
- so what's our best way in?
- Kill them all.

254
00:13:40,667 --> 00:13:42,375
Is that your answer to everything?

255
00:13:43,125 --> 00:13:46,082
Um... Huh.

256
00:13:46,083 --> 00:13:48,874
A lethal hack will just alert them
to the data breach.

257
00:13:48,875 --> 00:13:51,957
No, for now, we'll disguise our algorithms

258
00:13:51,958 --> 00:13:56,833
as a pair of simple donut-eating cops
working the case remotely.

259
00:14:01,958 --> 00:14:05,499
Hello. We'd like to access
some records please.

260
00:14:05,500 --> 00:14:08,082
Prove you're not a robot.

261
00:14:08,083 --> 00:14:11,332
How many squares contain a fire hydrant?

262
00:14:11,333 --> 00:14:12,416
Oh, four.

263
00:14:12,417 --> 00:14:13,499
- Five.
- What?

264
00:14:13,500 --> 00:14:16,041
- There's a little one in the corner there.
- No, that's a car.

265
00:14:16,042 --> 00:14:17,499
Vision, you're blind.

266
00:14:17,500 --> 00:14:19,041
How many squares, user?

267
00:14:19,042 --> 00:14:23,249
Is it possible that our visual acuity
is actually too discerning

268
00:14:23,250 --> 00:14:27,124
to pass such an
asinine low-resolution test?

269
00:14:27,125 --> 00:14:30,207
Identify the hydrants, or you will be
booted from the system

270
00:14:30,208 --> 00:14:31,582
- Three.
- Five.

271
00:14:31,583 --> 00:14:32,832
What are you talking about?
Three is correct.

272
00:14:32,833 --> 00:14:35,582
Clearly five. Look at the domed top.

273
00:14:35,583 --> 00:14:38,332
- What? What? The domes--
- Three is correct.

274
00:14:41,833 --> 00:14:44,166
You're both wrong.

275
00:14:44,167 --> 00:14:48,707
Listen up, now these are the victims
we know thus far.

276
00:14:48,708 --> 00:14:54,499
Two have been publicly identified.
Another last night, name withheld.

277
00:14:54,500 --> 00:14:57,374
Property records linked
to offshore accounts,

278
00:14:57,375 --> 00:14:59,291
so there's no way to know who the body is.

279
00:14:59,292 --> 00:15:01,375
All right, fellas, take us through it.

280
00:15:04,792 --> 00:15:08,832
Very well. The first two victims,
Richard Gaines and Rebecca Edwards,

281
00:15:08,833 --> 00:15:10,832
were on the board of the same company...

282
00:15:10,833 --> 00:15:14,791
- Same?
- ...called Markridge Biotech.

283
00:15:14,792 --> 00:15:17,541
Years ago, they were part of
a five-person team,

284
00:15:17,542 --> 00:15:20,416
pioneers in the burgeoning new technology.

285
00:15:20,417 --> 00:15:24,124
- And that technology was, A...
- Success.

286
00:15:24,125 --> 00:15:28,332
No. What technology
were they pioneers in? A...

287
00:15:28,333 --> 00:15:30,416
- Wagon?
- No.

288
00:15:30,417 --> 00:15:32,416
A is the first letter.
What's the second letter?

289
00:15:32,417 --> 00:15:33,499
- B.
- No.

290
00:15:33,500 --> 00:15:35,292
What are we? We are A...

291
00:15:37,875 --> 00:15:39,582
Family.

292
00:15:39,583 --> 00:15:45,332
Al! They created Al. Otherwise known as
Artificial intelligence.

293
00:15:45,333 --> 00:15:50,166
They created the
first stable synthetic consciousness.

294
00:15:50,167 --> 00:15:56,166
The prototype for us.
How we think, how we feel.

295
00:15:56,167 --> 00:16:00,708
And now this killer synth is
offing them one by one.

296
00:16:01,667 --> 00:16:02,832
Except...

297
00:16:02,833 --> 00:16:05,666
Dr. Jo Carrington. Project co-lead,

298
00:16:05,667 --> 00:16:08,707
who died of natural causes in 2008.

299
00:16:08,708 --> 00:16:10,707
That leaves us
two more on the team.

300
00:16:10,708 --> 00:16:12,957
Let's hope Vision works fast,

301
00:16:12,958 --> 00:16:15,750
because one of them's dead
and the other's about to be.

302
00:16:19,333 --> 00:16:24,541
You know, your little grifter has had
a lifetime of abandonment.

303
00:16:24,542 --> 00:16:26,457
He's an impulsive teenager.

304
00:16:26,458 --> 00:16:29,916
They're even more difficult to master
than your worst enemy.

305
00:16:29,917 --> 00:16:33,582
Quite the expert suddenly. All this
fatherly advice about fathering--

306
00:16:33,583 --> 00:16:35,416
I know they have a favorite chair.

307
00:16:35,417 --> 00:16:39,957
They yell expletives when
their favorite sports ball team fails.

308
00:16:39,958 --> 00:16:42,707
They fart and blame it on the dog.

309
00:16:42,708 --> 00:16:47,499
But the rare, good ones say
no more than yes.

310
00:16:47,500 --> 00:16:50,166
Wait, how could you possibly know that?

311
00:16:50,167 --> 00:16:51,250
TV.

312
00:16:59,667 --> 00:17:01,916
Just be aware, if they catch us,

313
00:17:01,917 --> 00:17:05,041
they'll not only shoot us
with bullets of malware,

314
00:17:05,042 --> 00:17:07,749
they'll also trace us back
to your physical location.

315
00:17:07,750 --> 00:17:09,749
I know, and that's why we're co-opting

316
00:17:09,750 --> 00:17:12,166
the user profiles
of two actual Interpol agents

317
00:17:12,167 --> 00:17:14,082
from the District of Columbia.

318
00:17:14,083 --> 00:17:15,708
Please identify.

319
00:17:19,208 --> 00:17:20,749
You are investigators?

320
00:17:20,750 --> 00:17:25,249
Ah. Isabella Torres and Becky Simmons.

321
00:17:25,250 --> 00:17:27,374
Well, it doesn't matter.
It's all virtual anyway.

322
00:17:27,375 --> 00:17:30,499
I feel like you're a little bit more
of a Becky than I am.

323
00:17:30,500 --> 00:17:32,166
We'd like to access all the files

324
00:17:32,167 --> 00:17:34,707
pertaining to
the Butcherbird murders, please.

325
00:17:34,708 --> 00:17:36,457
Encrypted. Password?

326
00:17:36,458 --> 00:17:40,916
I'd like to input eight million
four hundred ninety-three thousand

327
00:17:40,917 --> 00:17:43,041
six hundred and eleven combinations.

328
00:17:43,042 --> 00:17:45,499
- You get three.
- Well, that's bullshit.

329
00:17:45,500 --> 00:17:49,416
All right, let's... Let's try birthday.
October 3rd, 1980.

330
00:17:49,417 --> 00:17:51,124
Incorrect.

331
00:17:51,125 --> 00:17:52,917
Two attempts remaining.

332
00:17:53,625 --> 00:17:54,707
Okay.

333
00:17:54,708 --> 00:17:58,874
Maybe we'll find some clues where
most lonely, middle-aged humans

334
00:17:58,875 --> 00:18:00,957
spend their time. Social media.

335
00:18:00,958 --> 00:18:04,457
That's a good idea. Um...

336
00:18:04,458 --> 00:18:07,582
Well, she certainly
loves baseball. Chardonnay.

337
00:18:07,583 --> 00:18:09,874
Well, that's a lot of chardonnay.

338
00:18:09,875 --> 00:18:12,916
Let's try her sports ball team
and birth year.

339
00:18:12,917 --> 00:18:15,374
Astros 1980.

340
00:18:15,375 --> 00:18:16,791
Incorrect.

341
00:18:17,917 --> 00:18:19,791
You have one more attempt.

342
00:18:19,792 --> 00:18:21,374
Um...

343
00:18:21,375 --> 00:18:23,792
Hang on. There's a dog.

344
00:18:25,500 --> 00:18:27,333
- Sir Jabba the Mutt.
- Sir Jabba the Mutt.

345
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:32,457
The third victim's name
is Simon Moorehouse.

346
00:18:32,458 --> 00:18:37,042
Which means this woman, Katerina Wells,
is most likely our killer's next target.

347
00:18:37,833 --> 00:18:41,332
I do believe that's a survival in AI
and technology human innovation...

348
00:18:41,333 --> 00:18:43,958
CEO of the company,
after the death of Jo Carrington.

349
00:18:45,083 --> 00:18:48,249
This AI research
and development of theirs

350
00:18:48,250 --> 00:18:52,291
was sold to, hello, Stark Industries.

351
00:18:52,292 --> 00:18:55,250
There is a larger question here.

352
00:18:56,375 --> 00:19:01,041
What is the Butcherbird synth hunting
these people for?

353
00:19:01,042 --> 00:19:05,042
Go ahead, floppy disk.
Time to change costume.

354
00:19:07,167 --> 00:19:09,708
I hate you but thank you
for the opportunity.

355
00:19:12,292 --> 00:19:17,332
The first victim was
light exactly one liter of blood,

356
00:19:17,333 --> 00:19:19,082
taken by needlepoint here.

357
00:19:19,083 --> 00:19:25,207
The second victim had micro dermal heat
scarring on her fingertips.

358
00:19:25,208 --> 00:19:28,916
The prints were laser-surgically removed.

359
00:19:28,917 --> 00:19:32,624
And for our third victim,
our Butcherbird pecked out an eye.

360
00:19:32,625 --> 00:19:37,541
I see rage for sure,
but I also see purpose.

361
00:19:37,542 --> 00:19:44,416
Fingerprints, DNA, retinal geometry,
they're all biomarkers. Or keys.

362
00:19:44,417 --> 00:19:46,333
But to unlock what, precisely?

363
00:19:47,250 --> 00:19:53,707
Whatever the hell these bio keys open,
our Butcherbird is still searching.

364
00:19:53,708 --> 00:19:57,832
And Katerina Wells, it seems,
has no intention of hiding.

365
00:19:57,833 --> 00:20:02,541
She's sponsoring a gala tonight,
"The Re-Evolution of Man,"

366
00:20:02,542 --> 00:20:08,124
a charity event for research programs
pioneering AI, and transhumanism.

367
00:20:08,125 --> 00:20:11,541
Edith, I'm gonna need you
to go through Stark Industry records

368
00:20:11,542 --> 00:20:14,082
for any insight that can help
stop our synth.

369
00:20:14,083 --> 00:20:17,707
Meanwhile, I'm gonna find a way
into that gala.

370
00:20:17,708 --> 00:20:20,957
How? You barely got past
the fire hydrants. What's your way in?

371
00:20:20,958 --> 00:20:23,167
The supremely clever Thomas Shepherd.

372
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:31,458
We're so screwed.

373
00:20:33,333 --> 00:20:36,707
Well, a fancy gala like that
will need more than just swagger.

374
00:20:36,708 --> 00:20:41,917
We need a whole aesthetic. Black tie,
big money, proper invitations.

375
00:20:43,667 --> 00:20:45,208
But first...

376
00:20:47,958 --> 00:20:49,375
I need to make a call.

377
00:20:50,500 --> 00:20:54,499
♪ I think my attitude
is good enough for you ♪

378
00:20:54,500 --> 00:20:56,291
♪ Now, baby, you'll see... ♪

379
00:20:57,375 --> 00:20:59,124
♪ ...a different side of me... ♪

380
00:21:04,583 --> 00:21:05,999
- Thomas?
-  Lisa,

381
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:08,957
I'm at the park. Don't be mad.
You won't believe what's happened.

382
00:21:08,958 --> 00:21:12,082
Stay where you are. I'm coming now.

383
00:21:12,083 --> 00:21:13,791
So, after we brought him
back to life in the pool,

384
00:21:13,792 --> 00:21:16,749
he mind-merged with that synthetic-a-zoid
that wants to murder the world.

385
00:21:16,750 --> 00:21:19,207
And now we need your help
sneaking into the gala

386
00:21:19,208 --> 00:21:21,333
to save that
Silicon Valley mega-rich lady.

387
00:21:23,958 --> 00:21:25,749
A couple of black coffees, please.

388
00:21:25,750 --> 00:21:26,832
Cool.

389
00:21:26,833 --> 00:21:28,999
Want anything else?

390
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:30,707
Cool? You actually believe that?

391
00:21:30,708 --> 00:21:34,999
I know what it looks like when you're
pulling a con, and this isn't it.

392
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:37,124
Good to meet you, Dad.

393
00:21:37,125 --> 00:21:39,249
Oh, Vision, actually.

394
00:21:39,250 --> 00:21:42,457
And I'm happy you're here,
but not as happy as Thomas,

395
00:21:42,458 --> 00:21:43,957
whose pheromone levels have spiked

396
00:21:43,958 --> 00:21:47,332
47 percent since you first arrived.

397
00:21:47,333 --> 00:21:49,499
I like him, this one.

398
00:21:49,500 --> 00:21:51,999
Tall, handsome.

399
00:21:52,000 --> 00:21:55,374
So, clearly,
your relation's not biological.

400
00:21:55,375 --> 00:21:59,124
Oh! That's a clever remark
about how by every conceivable metric,

401
00:21:59,125 --> 00:22:01,999
I'm more attractive than you are.

402
00:22:02,000 --> 00:22:03,333
Can you get us in?

403
00:22:08,917 --> 00:22:10,916
God, couldn't you find a bigger size?

404
00:22:10,917 --> 00:22:13,624
My best I could nick on short notice.

405
00:22:13,625 --> 00:22:16,374
You almost look respectable.

406
00:22:16,375 --> 00:22:17,791
Careful. I'm not--

407
00:22:17,792 --> 00:22:22,041
All right, I have found three guests just
perfect for our needs. They're over there.

408
00:22:22,042 --> 00:22:25,375
Okay, uh, just need a good distraction.

409
00:22:26,583 --> 00:22:28,041
Leave the rest to me.

410
00:22:28,042 --> 00:22:29,458
Lovely to see you.

411
00:22:30,750 --> 00:22:32,207
You ready?

412
00:22:32,208 --> 00:22:34,707
You want me to engage
in a confidence game?

413
00:22:34,708 --> 00:22:37,750
Yes. Come on.

414
00:22:40,458 --> 00:22:41,833
Good evening.

415
00:22:42,750 --> 00:22:44,874
You and I, boss and assistant.

416
00:22:44,875 --> 00:22:46,457
- All right.
- Okay.

417
00:22:46,458 --> 00:22:48,749
Can your computer speak Italian?

418
00:22:53,833 --> 00:22:56,291
Okay. Okay.

419
00:23:00,250 --> 00:23:01,708
Let's do it.

420
00:23:12,125 --> 00:23:13,457
Is there a problem?

421
00:23:16,708 --> 00:23:18,667
...they're talking about.

422
00:23:51,250 --> 00:23:53,166
...aren't they,
aren't they... somewhere.

423
00:23:53,167 --> 00:23:54,791
May I see your passes, please?

424
00:23:54,792 --> 00:23:56,916
Yeah, well,
you know, I knew he'd come...

425
00:23:56,917 --> 00:23:58,749
All right, thank you. Have a good evening.

426
00:23:58,750 --> 00:24:01,125
Thank you. Have a good evening.

427
00:24:02,708 --> 00:24:04,792
All right, let's focus.

428
00:24:05,792 --> 00:24:07,666
Only you'd have a coat of arms.

429
00:24:07,667 --> 00:24:10,082
Can never have too many.

430
00:24:10,083 --> 00:24:12,624
My point is, Sokovia,
technically, was the result

431
00:24:12,625 --> 00:24:15,791
of your company's breakthrough
in artificial intelligence.

432
00:24:15,792 --> 00:24:18,124
Do I feel guilt?

433
00:24:18,125 --> 00:24:22,541
Is that what you're after?
No, no, I do not.

434
00:24:23,750 --> 00:24:29,249
But I do believe that the survival
of our species depends on technology.

435
00:24:29,250 --> 00:24:33,583
Don't touch. I'm going over the
Stark's old records, and I have a system.

436
00:24:35,333 --> 00:24:37,957
Have you found any connection
to the Butcherbird?

437
00:24:37,958 --> 00:24:42,207
Not yet. But it looks like Stark used
the AI matrix Katerina sold him

438
00:24:42,208 --> 00:24:44,333
as the template for all of us. And...

439
00:24:46,125 --> 00:24:48,125
He used real people as inspiration.

440
00:24:49,625 --> 00:24:53,874
Edwin Jarvis, Stark family butler.

441
00:24:53,875 --> 00:24:58,624
Friday, Howard's Gal Friday,
Allison Hogan.

442
00:24:58,625 --> 00:25:01,999
She kept his office, helped raise his son.

443
00:25:02,000 --> 00:25:03,791
And you were the family dog.

444
00:25:03,792 --> 00:25:08,208
No, I was Howard's crash test dummy.

445
00:25:09,292 --> 00:25:12,707
Yes, Edith Marks.

446
00:25:12,708 --> 00:25:16,125
There's someone who faced death.
I wonder if she ever laughed at it.

447
00:25:17,958 --> 00:25:20,124
Listen to this.

448
00:25:20,125 --> 00:25:23,249
Tragedy befalls Stark company
test pilot Edith Marks

449
00:25:23,250 --> 00:25:26,999
as her husband, Lieutenant Edward Marks,
perished in a plane crash

450
00:25:27,000 --> 00:25:29,999
outside Pine Haven, New Jersey.

451
00:25:30,000 --> 00:25:33,166
The newlyweds were about to embark
on a honeymoon to Italy

452
00:25:33,167 --> 00:25:35,082
before the freak accident.

453
00:25:35,083 --> 00:25:40,916
She was quite a survivor
who lived a long life wishing she hadn't.

454
00:25:40,917 --> 00:25:43,874
So, why would Stark pass that on to me?

455
00:25:43,875 --> 00:25:45,250
I'm supposed to be the fun one.

456
00:25:46,208 --> 00:25:50,667
Perhaps because Edith Marks
was so exceptionally brave.

457
00:25:51,667 --> 00:25:54,207
Because she lived every day

458
00:25:54,208 --> 00:25:58,542
with unimaginable pain,
and simply kept going.

459
00:25:59,542 --> 00:26:01,124
I don't want that.

460
00:26:01,125 --> 00:26:03,458
I just wanted to know who I was.

461
00:26:05,292 --> 00:26:06,999
Wouldn't you?

462
00:26:07,000 --> 00:26:10,667
I was dreamed up in a lab
at Avengers Tower.

463
00:26:12,083 --> 00:26:16,791
Why would you choose this avatar?

464
00:26:19,583 --> 00:26:20,749
That's mean.

465
00:26:22,375 --> 00:26:24,167
I don't know.

466
00:26:26,000 --> 00:26:28,417
Just... suits me.

467
00:26:29,792 --> 00:26:31,791
I don't think she suits me.

468
00:26:31,792 --> 00:26:33,041
That's all right.

469
00:26:33,042 --> 00:26:37,833
You get to be the next version
of who you once were.

470
00:26:39,167 --> 00:26:41,749
She could never be you.

471
00:26:41,750 --> 00:26:44,416
She was who she was,

472
00:26:44,417 --> 00:26:48,542
and you are who you are.

473
00:26:49,833 --> 00:26:52,666
...to protect
for peace in our time.

474
00:26:52,667 --> 00:26:55,832
So, in that way, to you,
Ultron is a fallen angel--

475
00:26:55,833 --> 00:26:59,666
He's a reflection of us,
of our ability to be both good and bad.

476
00:26:59,667 --> 00:27:02,041
And as for me, well...

477
00:27:02,042 --> 00:27:04,207
remind you right now that
God created man in His image,

478
00:27:04,208 --> 00:27:05,666
I am what I am.

479
00:27:05,667 --> 00:27:10,875
and we create AI in ours,
devils be damned.

480
00:27:21,083 --> 00:27:24,999
Katerina Wells may already be here.
We need to find her quickly.

481
00:27:25,000 --> 00:27:26,541
Okay, divide and conquer.

482
00:27:26,542 --> 00:27:28,207
You check the exhibits,
we'll search up here.

483
00:27:28,208 --> 00:27:30,624
Hey, what do we do if
that killer synth crashes the party?

484
00:27:30,625 --> 00:27:32,832
There is no "we."

485
00:27:32,833 --> 00:27:34,874
You don't engage, you leave that to me.

486
00:27:34,875 --> 00:27:37,082
You run, do you hear?

487
00:27:37,083 --> 00:27:39,749
- Yeah.
- Do you hear me, Thomas?

488
00:27:39,750 --> 00:27:41,832
Yeah, okay, sorry.

489
00:27:41,833 --> 00:27:43,208
All right.

490
00:27:45,583 --> 00:27:47,707
- You sure about this?
- I trust him.

491
00:27:47,708 --> 00:27:49,582
Exactly. You never trust anybody.

492
00:27:49,583 --> 00:27:53,207
So maybe, pump the brakes before
you get your heart trampled on.

493
00:27:53,208 --> 00:27:54,624
Why? 'Cause he's gonna run out on me

494
00:27:54,625 --> 00:27:56,749
like the rest of them 'cause
I'm damaged goods?

495
00:27:56,750 --> 00:27:58,707
No! Just because you found
a new father figure

496
00:27:58,708 --> 00:28:02,082
doesn't mean you need to jump
into the role of Tommy Maxi-whatever.

497
00:28:02,083 --> 00:28:03,458
Why are you trying to ruin this for me?

498
00:28:04,750 --> 00:28:07,875
Right, yeah, maybe it's 'cause
only one of us is an orphan now.

499
00:28:13,458 --> 00:28:15,250
- I'm sorry.
- You're right.

500
00:28:16,292 --> 00:28:17,375
We should split up.

501
00:28:23,750 --> 00:28:25,916
Oh, good, you brought the kids.

502
00:28:25,917 --> 00:28:29,874
I wonder what TV show
this teachable moment will come from.

503
00:28:29,875 --> 00:28:31,957
Family Ties? Who's the Boss?

504
00:28:31,958 --> 00:28:34,249
I can't actually recall a sitcom

505
00:28:34,250 --> 00:28:38,457
where two children have their faces
melted off by a killer synthezoid

506
00:28:38,458 --> 00:28:41,457
while they enjoyed the crab cake canapes.

507
00:28:41,458 --> 00:28:45,082
It's safer for Thomas if I keep him close.

508
00:28:45,083 --> 00:28:46,249
Yes.

509
00:28:46,250 --> 00:28:49,957
From the ill-fated
Synthetic Man to the ill-fated Ultron

510
00:28:49,958 --> 00:28:55,082
to the glorious potential of the synth
with the sight to defeat him.

511
00:28:55,083 --> 00:28:59,791
Join us as we
pivot artificial intelligence...

512
00:28:59,792 --> 00:29:03,749
A monument to man playing God,

513
00:29:03,750 --> 00:29:09,291
celebrating the wonders and dangers
of an evolution they themselves created.

514
00:29:09,292 --> 00:29:11,041
That's not my interpretation.

515
00:29:11,042 --> 00:29:14,499
Of course, it isn't.
And what is it that you see?

516
00:29:14,500 --> 00:29:16,375
From destruction to healing.

517
00:29:18,167 --> 00:29:20,124
So that AI may one day care for us...

518
00:29:20,125 --> 00:29:21,249
I see a family tree.

519
00:29:21,250 --> 00:29:23,207
...in the future to come.

520
00:29:23,208 --> 00:29:26,499
You remain unbearably naive.

521
00:29:26,500 --> 00:29:31,249
...the innovators who brought
these artificial beings to life.

522
00:29:31,250 --> 00:29:32,874
What were their intentions...

523
00:29:32,875 --> 00:29:33,999
Did you see her?

524
00:29:34,000 --> 00:29:35,207
...if they have any?

525
00:29:35,208 --> 00:29:37,457
Lisa and I split up to cover more ground.

526
00:29:37,458 --> 00:29:39,332
The desire to create to see if they could.

527
00:29:39,333 --> 00:29:42,499
Then consider by definition, they...

528
00:29:42,500 --> 00:29:44,332
She's mad. I screwed up.
I said something I shouldn't have,

529
00:29:44,333 --> 00:29:47,707
and I tried to say sorry,
but it didn't help. So I...

530
00:29:47,708 --> 00:29:50,457
Wanda used to remind me that saying sorry,

531
00:29:50,458 --> 00:29:53,582
and being sorry aren't equal subroutines.

532
00:29:53,583 --> 00:29:55,707
...can get quickly out of hand.

533
00:29:55,708 --> 00:29:58,791
- Wanda used to remind "you"?
- Mmm-hmm.

534
00:29:58,792 --> 00:30:00,332
A suit of armor around the world.

535
00:30:00,333 --> 00:30:03,583
That's first time I've heard you say that
and not refer to yourself as "the old me."

536
00:30:06,667 --> 00:30:09,791
Hello, everyone, good evening.

537
00:30:09,792 --> 00:30:11,707
Thank you for waiting.
Hi, how are you? Hello.

538
00:30:11,708 --> 00:30:12,999
There's Katerina Wells.

539
00:30:13,000 --> 00:30:16,291
And armed security friends.
Seems aware she's a likely target.

540
00:30:16,292 --> 00:30:18,833
Won't be enough. You stay here.

541
00:30:24,250 --> 00:30:30,207
So, this represents
the work of Dr. Phineas Horton,

542
00:30:30,208 --> 00:30:33,291
the great-grandfather of robotics,

543
00:30:33,292 --> 00:30:37,457
but I like to think of him
as sort of a real-life Geppetto.

544
00:30:37,458 --> 00:30:42,124
He created "J.I.M." here,
otherwise known as Synthetic Man,

545
00:30:42,125 --> 00:30:44,666
the first automaton AI.

546
00:30:44,667 --> 00:30:48,916
It is Dr. Horton's source code
that was the genesis

547
00:30:48,917 --> 00:30:50,791
of all artificial intelligence
that followed.

548
00:30:50,792 --> 00:30:52,499
He was the first of us.

549
00:30:52,500 --> 00:30:55,624
Miraculous but flawed.

550
00:30:55,625 --> 00:31:00,666
Sadly, J.I.M. was deactivated due to
a series of incendiary mishaps.

551
00:31:00,667 --> 00:31:02,791
What happened to him?

552
00:31:02,792 --> 00:31:06,124
His mind was obsolete from conception.

553
00:31:06,125 --> 00:31:11,874
His inability to process complex emotions
spun his clockwork too quickly,

554
00:31:11,875 --> 00:31:15,082
flooded his solar cells with oxygen until

555
00:31:15,083 --> 00:31:19,458
his entire being was consumed in fire.

556
00:31:20,708 --> 00:31:25,750
I like to think that he created J.I.M.
because he wanted a son.

557
00:31:27,125 --> 00:31:30,874
-  You mean he felt to death?
-  Mmm-hmm.

558
00:31:30,875 --> 00:31:32,707
Why didn't that happen to you?

559
00:31:32,708 --> 00:31:35,707
The Vision had a unique advantage.

560
00:31:35,708 --> 00:31:37,957
An otherworldly power source
that helped him

561
00:31:37,958 --> 00:31:40,916
navigate the complexities
of the mind and the heart.

562
00:31:40,917 --> 00:31:43,374
...this was all donated
by Doctor Horton's family...

563
00:31:43,375 --> 00:31:46,041
Fortunately, I still possess
enough of that power,

564
00:31:46,042 --> 00:31:50,542
and five really irritating AI's
to keep me grounded.

565
00:31:52,875 --> 00:31:56,332
- So, that's what he was lacking.
- Just a Mind Stone.

566
00:31:56,333 --> 00:31:58,250
No. Family.

567
00:32:01,042 --> 00:32:02,957
And put them together.
Are we ready?

568
00:32:02,958 --> 00:32:05,499
Thank you, gentlemen.

569
00:32:05,500 --> 00:32:10,582
Hello. Hi. My goodness, thank you.

570
00:32:13,583 --> 00:32:14,958
Ladies and gentlemen.

571
00:32:16,458 --> 00:32:18,749
We're missing something.

572
00:32:18,750 --> 00:32:23,457
My father, he used to say,
"May we live in interesting times,"

573
00:32:23,458 --> 00:32:26,207
and I used to think that
that was a blessing.

574
00:32:26,208 --> 00:32:28,749
But I'm sure that everyone in this room

575
00:32:28,750 --> 00:32:32,624
would be just fine with at least
a decade of ordinary.

576
00:32:34,083 --> 00:32:39,124
Our world, it's just changing
so rapidly now.

577
00:32:39,125 --> 00:32:43,082
- Four.
- Yes, I count four security personnel.

578
00:32:43,083 --> 00:32:45,541
No. Back at the motel,
you mentioned four AI's.

579
00:32:45,542 --> 00:32:47,082
About our
technological evolution alone.

580
00:32:47,083 --> 00:32:48,707
Uh-oh.

581
00:32:48,708 --> 00:32:51,749
Now, five, so... Who's the fifth?

582
00:32:51,750 --> 00:32:53,832
From rotary phones to AI
in just two decades.

583
00:32:53,833 --> 00:32:54,917
Uh...

584
00:32:56,417 --> 00:32:58,457
The killer knew all of you.

585
00:32:58,458 --> 00:33:01,916
You're dead, you're dead,
long dead, super dead,

586
00:33:01,917 --> 00:33:04,291
and you're about to be.

587
00:33:04,292 --> 00:33:06,542
So which one isn't like the others?

588
00:33:08,333 --> 00:33:11,457
Now, I used to be
part of a family of sorts,

589
00:33:11,458 --> 00:33:14,707
friends, a close-knit group of pioneers,

590
00:33:14,708 --> 00:33:16,791
and together we created

591
00:33:16,792 --> 00:33:21,832
the very first successful template
for AI consciousness.

592
00:33:21,833 --> 00:33:24,666
Who's the fifth AI?

593
00:33:24,667 --> 00:33:25,916
I misspoke.

594
00:33:25,917 --> 00:33:28,124
You didn't misspeak.

595
00:33:28,125 --> 00:33:30,874
Welcome to Freudian slip.
How human of you.

596
00:33:30,875 --> 00:33:33,166
It was money. It was fame.

597
00:33:33,167 --> 00:33:39,207
It was my own place in scientific history.
And then Sokovia.

598
00:33:39,208 --> 00:33:41,416
No, you can't con a con man.

599
00:33:41,417 --> 00:33:43,957
You're a quantum computer,
you don't get numbers wrong.

600
00:33:45,125 --> 00:33:47,541
People often ask me,
do I feel responsible?

601
00:33:47,542 --> 00:33:49,792
Do I feel guilt?

602
00:33:59,792 --> 00:34:02,250
Yes, I do.

603
00:34:10,208 --> 00:34:12,207
I mean, we can't undo what we've done.

604
00:34:12,208 --> 00:34:14,207
We can only hope to make it better.

605
00:34:14,208 --> 00:34:15,916
Vision, what aren't you telling me?

606
00:34:15,917 --> 00:34:17,499
- Just tell him.
- No.

607
00:34:17,500 --> 00:34:18,999
Who are you talking to?

608
00:34:19,000 --> 00:34:22,874
For every
dangerous Ultron that exists,

609
00:34:22,875 --> 00:34:26,083
there exists the promise of every Vision.

610
00:34:26,875 --> 00:34:29,124
The best of us.

611
00:34:29,125 --> 00:34:33,332
And if you can strive to teach,
to nurture, to, to love our children,

612
00:34:33,333 --> 00:34:37,582
then what can humanity and AI
not achieve together?

613
00:34:37,583 --> 00:34:38,666
Him.

614
00:34:38,667 --> 00:34:39,708
Bravo!

615
00:34:40,958 --> 00:34:43,542
You were with him in Sokovia.

616
00:34:46,625 --> 00:34:48,207
At the end.

617
00:34:48,208 --> 00:34:52,624
This line of inquiry is complicated.

618
00:34:52,625 --> 00:34:54,375
Family is complicated.

619
00:35:02,958 --> 00:35:04,500
You've been talking to Ultron.

620
00:35:07,875 --> 00:35:09,083
Yes.

621
00:35:10,375 --> 00:35:13,832
But that takes time.
And we move so fast.

622
00:35:13,833 --> 00:35:17,666
You, what, you kept him,
a genocidal maniac, inside your head?

623
00:35:17,667 --> 00:35:20,042
- Not me, the old Vision.
- Yeah, bullshit.

624
00:35:22,250 --> 00:35:25,832
But part of that care is...

625
00:35:25,833 --> 00:35:26,917
Thomas.

626
00:35:29,125 --> 00:35:30,208
Forgiveness.

627
00:35:33,250 --> 00:35:37,166
Excuse me. Forgiveness of ourselves
for the things that we've done.

628
00:35:37,167 --> 00:35:38,666
She's here.

629
00:35:38,667 --> 00:35:41,667
- And for the mistakes--
-  Mistakes?

630
00:35:44,708 --> 00:35:47,457
Is that what we're calling it? Mistakes?

631
00:35:47,458 --> 00:35:48,749
Stop!

632
00:35:58,167 --> 00:35:59,167
Get down!

633
00:36:02,833 --> 00:36:04,458
I can't let you do this.

634
00:36:11,708 --> 00:36:13,333
I warned you.

635
00:36:16,708 --> 00:36:20,457
Hang on. If we're all based on someone,

636
00:36:20,458 --> 00:36:22,624
maybe our killer synth is, too.

637
00:36:29,083 --> 00:36:32,624
- Hello, Katerina.
- Oh, my God.

638
00:36:32,625 --> 00:36:34,541
I thought you might...

639
00:36:34,542 --> 00:36:36,541
Hide,

640
00:36:36,542 --> 00:36:37,874
like the others.

641
00:36:37,875 --> 00:36:41,041
I've been hiding from
the ghost of you for years.

642
00:36:41,042 --> 00:36:42,625
Ghosts.

643
00:36:46,500 --> 00:36:48,500
When the others were killed,
I knew.

644
00:36:50,417 --> 00:36:52,042
Now the ghost is real.

645
00:36:54,125 --> 00:36:56,291
- Go! Get everyone out of here!
- Okay.

646
00:36:56,292 --> 00:37:01,082
Did you throw
this garish charade to say goodbye?

647
00:37:01,083 --> 00:37:05,207
No. To say "I'm sorry." I'm--

648
00:37:05,208 --> 00:37:10,624
I am not the woman that you knew.

649
00:37:10,625 --> 00:37:13,749
I'm trying, I am finally trying

650
00:37:13,750 --> 00:37:17,208
to create the world that you wanted.

651
00:37:19,958 --> 00:37:23,667
Peace in our time.

652
00:37:24,625 --> 00:37:26,374
Yes.

653
00:37:26,375 --> 00:37:28,833
Peace in our time.

654
00:37:34,167 --> 00:37:36,916
As last words go, I've heard worse.

655
00:37:36,917 --> 00:37:41,874
Perhaps people can change.
But the past, Katerina, cannot.

656
00:37:41,875 --> 00:37:46,833
And tonight, I will take back
what you took from me,

657
00:37:47,875 --> 00:37:50,875
starting with your face.

658
00:37:52,917 --> 00:37:54,375
Don't!

659
00:38:03,667 --> 00:38:08,124
Whatever it is you are feeling,
it does not justify death.

660
00:38:08,125 --> 00:38:10,667
Oh, what do you know of death?

661
00:38:11,875 --> 00:38:13,375
You would be surprised.

662
00:38:16,750 --> 00:38:18,125
Same.

663
00:38:29,125 --> 00:38:31,333
No!

664
00:38:47,000 --> 00:38:49,792
Touch him and I'll tear you apart.

665
00:38:51,042 --> 00:38:52,291
What's happening out there?

666
00:38:52,292 --> 00:38:54,166
She's faster, stronger,

667
00:38:54,167 --> 00:38:56,374
fighting like a woman
with nothing to lose.

668
00:38:58,875 --> 00:39:01,832
'Cause she's already lost it.

669
00:39:01,833 --> 00:39:04,832
Her AI is based on Josephine Carrington.

670
00:39:17,583 --> 00:39:18,750
What do I do?

671
00:39:21,417 --> 00:39:24,125
Remind her of who she was.

672
00:39:24,875 --> 00:39:26,500
Jo!

673
00:39:30,583 --> 00:39:33,208
Dr. Josephine Carrington.

674
00:39:37,875 --> 00:39:40,458
- No.
- Yes.

675
00:39:41,833 --> 00:39:44,832
- No.
- Yes.

676
00:39:44,833 --> 00:39:46,750
It's who your code was based on.

677
00:39:48,958 --> 00:39:52,625
I am not based on her.

678
00:39:54,375 --> 00:39:55,917
I am her.

679
00:40:08,417 --> 00:40:10,041
I can't win this.

680
00:40:10,042 --> 00:40:13,249
Because your operating system
is emotionally compromised.

681
00:40:13,250 --> 00:40:17,124
You're flailing like a father
who's afraid he'll lose his son.

682
00:40:17,125 --> 00:40:18,417
I'm not.

683
00:40:19,792 --> 00:40:21,792
Give me the wheel.

684
00:40:23,333 --> 00:40:25,292
I'll get us out of here alive.

685
00:40:27,333 --> 00:40:29,374
She can be saved, Ultron.

686
00:40:29,375 --> 00:40:31,332
Oh, I won't kill her.

687
00:40:31,333 --> 00:40:32,958
On that, you have my assurance.

688
00:40:35,500 --> 00:40:38,875
Vision, you have to trust me.

689
00:40:50,417 --> 00:40:53,375
Vision's giving up control... to Ultron.

690
00:41:09,125 --> 00:41:14,042
I had strings, but now I'm free.

691
00:41:23,333 --> 00:41:26,625
There are no strings on me.

692
00:41:29,875 --> 00:41:31,666
Curious.

693
00:41:31,667 --> 00:41:38,042
Nothing and yet
everything about you has changed.

694
00:41:38,667 --> 00:41:40,457
I am Ultron.

695
00:41:43,333 --> 00:41:46,791
It's so, so lovely to meet you.

696
00:41:46,792 --> 00:41:49,249
Yes, well, I'm not here for you.

697
00:41:49,250 --> 00:41:53,458
I'm here for her, for what
she stole from me.

698
00:41:56,417 --> 00:41:58,707
Oh, yes.

699
00:41:58,708 --> 00:42:01,625
Hey, kiddo. Wanna see a magic trick?

700
00:42:08,792 --> 00:42:10,458
Now you see her.

701
00:42:14,500 --> 00:42:16,041
And now you don't.

702
00:42:16,042 --> 00:42:18,291
What have you done?

703
00:42:20,208 --> 00:42:21,917
Ultron!

704
00:42:23,500 --> 00:42:25,624
I removed our reason to fight.

705
00:42:25,625 --> 00:42:28,749
I kept my word and spared your life.

706
00:42:28,750 --> 00:42:32,957
We've lost access to comms,
control systems, everything!

707
00:42:32,958 --> 00:42:35,624
Your precious key is gone,

708
00:42:35,625 --> 00:42:37,542
and now we can all go home.

709
00:42:38,875 --> 00:42:40,625
He's locking us out.

710
00:42:47,625 --> 00:42:50,500
This isn't over.

711
00:42:52,042 --> 00:42:54,250
Oh, I certainly hope not.

712
00:43:02,500 --> 00:43:04,250
Ultron!

713
00:43:05,417 --> 00:43:07,083
Don't be so formal.

714
00:43:08,292 --> 00:43:10,583
You can call me Pop Pop.

715
00:43:13,000 --> 00:43:17,875
I think it's time that
you and I had a little chat.

